        ],
        "explanation": "MetricAlertDetectorHandler now subclasses StatefulDetectorHandler with an empty body (`pass`). StatefulDetectorHandler declares abstract methods (get_dedupe_value, get_group_key_values, build_occurrence_and_event_data and others), and none of them are implemented. MetricAlertFire sets `detector_handler = MetricAlertDetectorHandler` (grouptype.py:27). `Detector.detector_handler` calls `group_type.detector_handler(self)` (models/detector.py:86), so a detector of type metric_alert_fire raises TypeError (\"Can't instantiate abstract class\"). The old class implemented `evaluate` and returned `[]`, so it could be instantiated.",
        "lines": {
          "end_line": 12,
          "start_line": 11
        },
